  "_note": "Real-world event calendar (the in-game Event Calendar). Not the same file as events.json, which lists the city's evt_* world events. The API upserts `events` into the `events` table (migration 085) and `questSets` drive POST /events/{slug}/progress. Real dates only, each with a primary source in `sourceUrl`. A time that the source does not state is stored as the whole UTC day (the event listing gives dates only). `streamUrl` is a link-out to the official stream, never embedded; it stays null until the organiser publishes one and ops set it with PUT /v1/admin/events/{slug}. Once ops edit an event, this file no longer overwrites that row. Interaction ids in `questSets` (booth, nod) are the ids the client sends as `proof.id`; the frontend owns the matching in-world objects and may add ids, never rename. Trivia answers are NOT in this file (server-only: contract/config/event_trivia.json). The `lanyard_breakpoint_2026` cosmetic is off-chain, never tradable, never an NFT.",
